{title: 427 - No Night There}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #427 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 427}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]In the land of [Ab7]fadeless [Db]day
[Gdim]Lies “the [Db]city [Ab7]four[Db]square;”
It shall never [C7]pass a[Db]way,
[Gdim]And there [Db]is “no [Ab7]night [Db]there.”
[Db]God shall “wipe a[Bb]way all [Ebm]tears;”
There’s no [Ab7]death, no pain, nor [Db]fears;
And they count not [Bbm]time by [Ebm]years,
[Gb7]For there [Db]is “no [Ab7]night [Db]there.”
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Db]God shall [Ab7]"wipe away [Db]all tears;"
[Gdim]There's [Db]no death, [Ab7]no pain, [Db]nor fears;
[C7]And they count [Db]not time by years,
[Gdim]For [Db]there is [Ab7]"no [Db]night there."
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]All the [Ab7]gates of [Db]pearl are made,
[Gdim]In [Db]"the [Ab7]city [Db]four-square;"
[C7]All the streets [Db]with gold are laid,
[Gdim]And [Db]there is [Ab7]"no [Db]night there."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]And the [Ab7]gates shall [Db]never close
[Gdim]To [Db]"the [Ab7]city [Db]four-square;"
[C7]There life's [Db]crystal river flows,
[Gdim]And [Db]there is [Ab7]"no [Db]night there."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db]There they [Ab7]need no [Db]sunshine bright,
[Gdim]In [Db]"that [Ab7]city [Db]four-square;"
[C7]For the Lamb [Db]is all the light,
[Gdim]And [Db]there is [Ab7]"no [Db]night there."
{end_of_verse}
